This extension adds DOOM Eternal modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.
[summary]EternalModInjector automatically installed.[/summary]

[b][color=#ffff00][size=3]AUGUST 2025 - DOOM Eternal has been updated to support mods natively through Bethesda.net. This extension can still be used to install "legacy" mods that use EternalModInjector.[/size][/color]
[size=3][b][color=#c27ba0]Game Pass Users - [/color][/b]You need to dump the game files according to the linked instructions in order to mod the game. This extension will download the ModInjector for you. You only need to dump the files -[b][url=https://gamebanana.com/posts/10737067] https://gamebanana.com/posts/10737067[/url][/b][/size][/b]

This extension will automatically download and install the [url=https://gamebanana.com/tools/7475]Doom Eternal Mod Injector[/url] at setup. This is required for legacy mods to work. This is version-dependent and will need to be updated for new game versions. Current version is: [b]Update 6.66 Rev. 3 N[/b].

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]GOG[/*]
[*]Epic[/*]
[*]Xbox[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Version Rollback mods with a "doometernalx64vk.exe" file install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]EternalModInjector mods with an "eternalmodmanager.exe" file install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Keep The Dead Eternal mods with a "keep the dead eternal - readme - install instructions.rtf" file install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Meath00k installs to the game folder, recognised by a "xinput1_3.dll" file.[/*]
[*]Nested Archive mods are supported.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*][size=2]For mods meant to go by the new modded executable, use mod type "SandBox (Modded Binaries)".[/size][/*]
[/list]

[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for DOOM Eternal mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Rollback:

Recognised when the archive contains a "doometernalx64vk.exe" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Injector:

Recognised when the archive contains a "eternalmodmanager.exe" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Ktde:

Recognised when the archive contains a "keep the dead eternal - readme - install instructions.rtf" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Meathook:

Recognised when the archive contains a "xinput1_3.dll" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Zip Mod:

Handled by the "testZipContent" installer. Inspect the extension source for the exact archive layout it expects.

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine.
[/spoiler]

